Subject: [PATCH] Count each contract once, as it stands today

HR keeps every version it records of a contract. Today's rewrite of the
mart counts contracts by their own dates and no longer keeps only the
version that holds today, so a tutor who moved to another unit this term
counts twice: in test tonight, the test each_contract_counts_once failed
on 3 contracts, and Nursing showed 67 teachers, 41 of them casual,
against HR's own 64 and 38.

This puts the clause back, as the project writes it (valid_at and
as_is_date, macros/shared/time.sql). Built and checked in my own schema
in test: every test passes, and Nursing counts 64 teachers, 38 of them
casual, as HR's report says. Nothing else changed.

Under the workload agent's mandate (governance/8-mandates/workload-agent.yml):
found, fixed and checked in test; for Jun Park to review.
---
 .../models/marts/workload/mart_workload__teaching_staff.sql    | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/films/analytics-engineering/project/models/marts/workload/mart_workload__teaching_staff.sql b/films/analytics-engineering/project/models/marts/workload/mart_workload__teaching_staff.sql
index 3b5d420..6120c01 100644
--- a/films/analytics-engineering/project/models/marts/workload/mart_workload__teaching_staff.sql
+++ b/films/analytics-engineering/project/models/marts/workload/mart_workload__teaching_staff.sql
@@ -19,6 +19,9 @@ contracts as (
 
     select *
     from {{ ref('stg_hr_system__contracts') }}
+    where {{ valid_at(as_is_date(),
+        'cast(recorded_from as date)',
+        'cast(recorded_to as date)') }}
 
 )
 
